0+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50616023/injured-florida-quarterback-aaron-philo-exits-3rd-quarter","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Akron coach Joe Moorhead resigns after 5 seasons to pursue other opportunities","description":"Akron head coach Joe Moorhead is stepping down after five seasons with the Zips to pursue other opportunities, he announced Friday.","published":"2026-11-27T21:03:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50614041/akron-coach-joe-moorhead-resigns-pursue-other-opportunities","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the winningest college football coaches of all time?","description":"From Saban to Paterno, there are many legendary college football coaches. Who has the best career record? Check out who has the most wins now.","published":"2026-11-27T20:18:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/39283806/who-winningest-college-football-coaches-all","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rivalry Week live: Top plays and playoff analysis","description":"It's the final week of the regular season. Here are the best plays, moments and CFP implications.","published":"2026-11-27T20:37:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50596213/rivalry-week-live-cfp-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 'College GameDay' Week 13: Duke vs. Wake Forest","description":"\"College GameDay\" heads to Wake Forest University for Week 13.","published":"2026-11-27T17:21:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50612493/2026-college-gameday-week-13-duke-vs-wake-forest","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"How every 2027 five-star college football prospect will fit","description":"There are 23 five-star players in the class, and we scout each one's game for the next level.","published":"2026-11-27T17:00:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/recruiting/story/_/id/48543549/college-football-recruiting-2027-prospects-five-star-scouts-take","type":"Story","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-27T15:51:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Houston, rivalry color rushes lead top uniforms of CFB Week 13","description":"Just because it's rivalry week doesn't mean teams still can't put their best foot forward with uniform swag.","published":"2026-11-27T15:00:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50598211/college-football-uniforms-week-13-houston","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5121819/luke-talich","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Talich"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Luke Talich","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luke_Talich","description":"American football safety (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-23T21:13:02Z","intro":"Lucas Wayne Talich (born July 7, 2004) is an American college football safety for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Talich grew up in Cody, Wyoming and attended Cody High School, where he played basketball and football and competed in track and field. As Cody's starting quarterback during his senior year, he passed for 1,682 yards while also rushing for 582 yards and accounted for 25 touchdowns. Talich was rated a three-star recruit and the top college prospect in Wyoming. He committed to play college football as a preferred walk-on for Notre Dame over scholarship offers from Washington State, Utah, and Wyoming."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Talich initially intended on redshirting his true freshman season at the University of Notre Dame, but due to injuries on defense and special teams played in the first eight games of the season before suffering a broken collarbone. He was awarded a scholarship during spring practices. Talich returned an interception 79 yards for a touchdown against Florida State during his sophomore year."}]}}